186	      <h3>✓ The source-side unlocks landed — the fleet moved from 20 → 35 fully-supported (rev 2)</h3>
187	      <p>Every build item from rev 2's §04 shipped across <strong>PR #524</strong> (composable auth, OData mode + <code>$metadata</code> discovery, incremental push-down) and <strong>PR #526</strong> (response-decode, async-job, scoped overwrite, <code>_faucet_*</code> metadata columns), plus the reshape transforms (#516) and discovery matrix (#501). Concretely:</p>
188	      <p><strong>Auth was the biggest unlock.</strong> The composable flow provider (#511 — login pre-flight, credential placement, request signing, OAuth1) cleared <strong>sap, acumatica, bullhorn, skyslope</strong> (session-cookie / dynamic-base-URL / HMAC) from Partial to Supported.</p>
189	      <p><strong>The two former "transport" blockers are now declarative.</strong> <strong>salesforce</strong> Bulk API (submit → poll → download CSV) is the async-job pattern (#514) + CSV decode (#515); <strong>oracle_fusion</strong>'s base64-XLSX-in-SOAP — the one case rev 2 flagged as WASM-only — is now the response-decode pipeline (#515: base64 → parse xlsx). <strong>No tap requires WASM.</strong></p>
190	      <p><strong>unpivot &amp; lookup are inbuilt now (#516)</strong>, so the eight "Needs SQL" rows whose only reshape was a wide→long unpivot or a reference-table join (anthropic, sharepointsites, onedrive, bamboohr, hibob, personio, deel, attio) are Supported inbuilt-only. And <strong>scoped overwrite (#518)</strong> decouples the report streams that used to <code>DELETE</code> a window from BigQuery (netsuite fully; quickbooks/xero/zohobooks entities).</p>
