264	    <h2><span class="num">04</span>Build backlog — fully delivered</h2>
265	    <p class="sub">Every build item across rounds 1–4 is now merged (✓). With <code>cross_join</code> (#534) and the ClickHouse/MSSQL staged-load execution (#528) landed in PR #537, there are <strong>no open follow-ups</strong>.</p>
266	    <ol class="build">
267	      <li><h3>Session / multi-step / signing auth provider <span class="who">— #511 ✓ PR #524 · unlocked sap · acumatica · bullhorn · skyslope · sage</span></h3><p>Login pre-flight (token / cookie / dynamic base-URL capture) + per-request signing (custom HMAC, OAuth1). Lives in <code>faucet-auth::flow::FlowProvider</code>, shared across rest / graphql / xml via the <code>auth: {ref}</code> catalog. Biggest single unlock.</p></li>
268	      <li><h3>Bookmark → request-parameter injection <span class="who">— #513 ✓ PR #524 · server-side incremental</span></h3><p><code>replication_bind</code> flows the stored bookmark into a query param / header / body / path (OData <code>$filter</code>, Lucene range, <code>gte|</code>, <code>If-Modified-Since</code>) with format control — so row counts match the taps that filter server-side.</p></li>
269	      <li><h3>Inbuilt <code>json_encode</code> + <code>unpivot</code> + <code>lookup</code> transforms <span class="who">— #516 ✓ PR #520 · removed the SQL dependency for 9 taps</span></h3><p><code>json_encode</code> stringifies a nested field to a STRING column; <code>unpivot</code> does wide→long; <code>lookup</code> joins a reference table. Together they moved anthropic, sharepoint, onedrive, bamboohr, hibob, personio, deel, attio to inbuilt-only.</p></li>
270	      <li><h3>Async-job source pattern + response decode <span class="who">— #514 &amp; #515 ✓ PR #526 · salesforce bulk · stripe reports · oracle_fusion</span></h3><p>Submit → poll <code>job_id</code> → fetch, feeding a decode pipeline (base64 / gunzip / unzip / parse csv·xlsx·xml). Reproduces the bulk-export shape and in-stream binary decode declaratively.</p></li>
271	      <li><h3>Report-stream decoupling via scoped overwrite <span class="who">— #518 ✓ PR #526 · netsuite · quickbooks · xero · zohobooks · sage</span></h3><p><code>write_mode: overwrite</code> with <code>scope: { window }</code> replaces only in-window rows atomically (postgres + bigquery), so a tap that <code>DELETE</code>s a rolling window then re-appends converges without the connector reaching into the warehouse.</p></li>
272	      <li><h3>Optional <code>_faucet_*</code> metadata columns <span class="who">— #510 ✓ PR #526</span></h3><p>Opt-in sink decorator stamping <code>_faucet_extracted_at</code> / <code>_loaded_at</code> / <code>_run_id</code> / <code>_source</code> / <code>_sequence</code>. faucet-native lineage (not required for parity since <code>_sdc</code> was dropped).</p></li>
273	      <li><h3>OData mode + <code>$metadata</code> / endpoint discovery + discovery matrix <span class="who">— #512 · #517 · #501 ✓ PRs #524 / earlier</span></h3><p>First-class OData paging/query, <code>$metadata</code>-driven <code>faucet discover</code>, and a discovery-driven request matrix (parent-child fan-out over dimensions fetched at plan time) — covering ms365bc, dualentry, rillet.</p></li>
274	      <li><h3>In-run datetime window slicing <span class="who">— #527 ✓ PR #532 · anthropic · deskera · navan · openai</span></h3><p>Bounds each request to a rolling <code>[start, end)</code> between the bookmark and <code>now</code>, iterating windows within one run with per-window bookmark durability. Airbyte <code>DatetimeBasedCursor</code> parity; capped/bounded date-range APIs no longer risk silent truncation on an unbounded incremental.</p></li>
275	      <li><h3>Inbuilt <code>tree_flatten</code> (recursive report-tree → rows) <span class="who">— #530 ✓ PR #532 · quickbooks · xero · zohobooks · rillet</span></h3><p>Walks a nested <code>Rows</code> structure, carries ancestor labels down, and emits one row per leaf with the period columns — moving the whole accounting-report cluster off the DuckDB SQL path to inbuilt.</p></li>
276	      <li><h3>Chained/two-level discovery + collected list dimensions <span class="who">— #531 ✓ PR #532 · hubspot (full custom-object support)</span></h3><p>A <code>discover:</code> row can itself <code>for_each:</code> an upstream dimension and publish the whole value-set per tuple (<code>collect: true</code>), injected comma-joined via <code>${id.alias}</code> — the discover-entities-then-fields shape (also Salesforce <code>describe</code>, Airtable, Notion).</p></li>
277	      <li><h3>Inbuilt <code>cross_join</code> transform <span class="who">— #534 ✓ PR #537 · ukg_pro → inbuilt</span></h3><p>The last SQL-only reshape: a cartesian product of sibling record-arrays within one record. Now a narrow inbuilt transform (fallible page-level, with a <code>max_product</code> guard), taking the fleet to 41 / 46 inbuilt-supported and 0 needing SQL.</p></li>
278	      <li><h3>Staged bulk load — ClickHouse / MSSQL <span class="who">— #528 ✓ PR #537 · execution complete</span></h3><p>The shared <code>faucet-core::staging</code> foundation merged in PR #532; PR #537 added the ClickHouse <code>s3()</code> / <code>gcs()</code> and MSSQL Azure-Blob <code>COPY INTO</code> execution paths (pure SQL/URL generators unit-tested; the wire execution isolated and excluded from coverage like the GCS/BigQuery data-plane). Redshift/Snowflake/BigQuery already loaded from an object store natively.</p></li>
279	    </ol>
